WEBVTT

p01
00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.230
Your AI agent writes the code.

p02
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.240
So why are you still updating your board...

p03
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:06.820
one click at a time?

p04
00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.280
Make it zero.

p05
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.020
Introducing the ZeroBoard MCP server.

p06
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:16.990
Free, and open source.

p07
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.730
Sign in once, and plug it into the agent you already use.

p08
00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:23.510
Just ask.

p09
00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:27.530
It plans the work, writes the cards, and builds the board.

p10
00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.240
Move tasks. Set due dates.

p11
00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.850
Check things off.

p12
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.590
Every change syncs live, and you never leave your editor.

p13
00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:43.700
Best of all?

p14
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:44.660
It's free.

p15
00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:46.860
Completely open source.

p16
00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:48.230
MIT licensed.

p17
00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:49.710
Read the code.

p18
00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:50.570
Fork it.

p19
00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:51.790
Self-host it.

p20
00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:55.640
Zero clicks.

p21
00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:56.920
Zero cost.

p22
00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.020
ZeroBoard.
